"""The concept data for the MonsterGirls families after the harpies (vol. I) and the anurans (vol. II).

One source of truth for the design: tools/build_field_guides.py renders it into <family>_field_guide.html, the model
scripts read the species ids / sizes / variant keys from it, and the Java side follows the numbers written here.

Every family shares the mod-wide relationship core (already in game for harpies and anurans):
  affection per player (feeding, petting, the family's own bond action) - 25 = high friendship (shares your bed,
  brings presents), 100 = full devotion (what a daughter feels for her father); a stick makes her sit; sharing a
  bed through the night starts a day-long pregnancy (her belly rounds out), and the family's own way of bearing
  young follows. Young are born devoted to the player who fathered them and never share that player's bed.

Rule from the design brief (2026-10-19): monster girls only, so clearly male-coded species or traits are swapped
for female ones (the lion becomes a lioness without a mane, the moose is dropped, no male courtship displays).
"""

TIERS = [
    ("Wild", "0", "Keeps her distance; her species' instincts decide everything."),
    ("Curious", "3+", "Lets you come close and watches what you do."),
    ("Fond", "10+", "Follows you a little way, accepts petting, stops fleeing."),
    ("High friendship", "25+", "May join you in bed at night (one night in three, more the fonder she is) and brings presents."),
    ("Devoted", "60+", "The family's devoted perk unlocks (see each guide)."),
    ("Full devotion", "100", "The most there is. Every daughter feels this for the player who fathered her."),
]

